<section class="review-section" id="faq">
<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"></line></svg> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Do I need DNA Center for Cisco AI Analytics?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Cisco AI Network Analytics runs as part of DNA Center (now Catalyst Center). You need to deploy the DNA Center appliance on-premise to use these features.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Does it work with non-Cisco devices?</div><div class="faq-answer">Limited. While DNA Center can discover and monitor some third-party devices, the AI analytics features work best with Cisco Catalyst and Meraki hardware. For multi-vendor environments, consider alternatives like Datadog or Splunk.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What's the difference from Meraki AI?</div><div class="faq-answer">Meraki has its own cloud-based AI features. DNA Center/Catalyst Center provides similar capabilities for on-premise Catalyst equipment. The two can integrate through the DNA-Meraki integration for unified visibility.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How long does deployment take?</div><div class="faq-answer">Initial DNA Center deployment typically takes 2-4 weeks for a large enterprise. Getting full value from AI analytics requires historical data collection, so expect 1-3 months before predictive features are fully trained.</div></div>
